    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by a tag that defines a custom comparator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The tag of <computeroutput>extension::compare_op</computeroutput> is a structure with a static <computeroutput>symbol</computeroutput>, which the failure reports write between the two operands, and a static <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput> member function template, which receives the operands, unwrapped, and returns the result of the comparison. The <computeroutput>symbol</computeroutput> must be printable, usually a <computeroutput>const char*</computeroutput> that includes the surrounding spaces; the result of <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput> must be convertible to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Tag_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the tag. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the left hand side operand, as <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput> receives it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the right hand side operand, as <computeroutput>apply()</computeroutput> receives it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
